      "value": "@{64e2bd1674393d094bec459c|full_name} \"Free\" isn't an age rating, there are plenty of Free to play Adult games on Steam for example.\n\nVRChat is a 13+ game, making it Rated T for Teen, but is often used for NSFW means even among those 17 and under. A method for locking down the NSFW content would be to Age Gate PC content. Basically make the game Quest Mode (extremely limited content) for anyone 17- and unlock PC Mode (Fully Featured) for those 18+.  That could jeopardize their Teen rating though, as the game would technically be rated for Everyone at that point, depending on the population of Fully Featured users it could even be considered a Mature game.\n\nBut due to basic human ingenuity, content restricting only creates an opportunity for someone to get around it. This would bring creative workarounds for those in the limited feature set to accomplish what they really want from the game.",
