      "value": "@{640c76efcced024514ae4d6a|full_name} I wrote a whole bunch more than 2500 characters apparently, and... only now do I see how old this comment is... ugh, just gonna delete the majority of it and say this:\n\nPeople agree to and accept data mining every day, even when subscribing to a cellular service, or buying a tablet, etc. Everything is always listening, curating ads, crunching keywords, taking hardware census data, even taking hardware sensor data too. These are things we all blindly agree to when installing apps and programs, and then later whine and complain about it happening.\n\nHonestly, it's getting old, your data is probably more secure in their hands than in yours anyways. Get over it.",
