      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Please, for the love of the gods. Age verification has been implemented but the fact that it requires a subscription is downright frustrating. I'm an adult. I'm not spending money on this game. But I don't want a teen in a friend group being exposed to adults speaking about--surprise, surprise!--adult topics because they saw us online and decided to join. How are we supposed to create an age-gated instance to protect children online if we have to pay money to age-gate it?\n\nThen I'm not really interested in NSFW content and would rather just filter it out. If it comes up in discussion in my friend group is one thing--seeing it at random in public spaces? Absolutely not.\n\nSetting a world to Invite+ is the only option we really have at the moment, and it's downright inconvenient. Has my friend group been biting the bullet and doing it? Yes. But not everyone on VRC will.",
